/// System-generated provenance for a memory or event: the owning actor and
/// session, and the creation and last-update timestamps. SearchMemories ,
/// SearchEvents , ListMemories , and GetMemory return the same block.
/// ListMemories and GetMemory always return createdAt and updatedAt . The
/// search operations return what is recorded and omit the block when
/// nothing is. In a query, the timestamps are system_metadata.created_at
/// and system_metadata.updated_at . Scope by owner with the top-level
/// parameters ( actorId on the search operations, actorIds on ListMemories
/// ) and sessionIds ( SearchEvents and ListMemories ). The search
/// operations reject actor and session fields inside the query or sort.
pub struct SystemMetadata {
  /// The owning actor. Absent when none was recorded.
  pub actor_id: Str? = None
  /// The owning session. Absent when none was recorded.
  pub session_id: Str? = None
  /// When the record was created. Always present on ListMemories and
  /// GetMemory . It can be absent from search results.
  pub created_at: Time? = None
  /// When the record was last updated. Equals createdAt for a record that has
  /// never been updated, and always for a SearchEvents result.
  pub updated_at: Time? = None
}

